euring's identity for $C_d$","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.DeuringCd, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.cdCoeff_eq_LFunction","summary":"For natural numbers $d$ and $n$ let $c_d(n)$ be the coefficients of the standard Euler product of $C_d$ and $\\lambda_d(n)$ the Hecke coefficients. *Deuring's identity* holds for $d$ if It says that $L(C_d,s)$ and the Hecke L-series $L(\\psi_d,s)$ have the same coefficients; it is proved below for every squarefree $d\\equiv1\\pmod4$, from Gauss's point count.","reading_title":{"format":"inline-parts-v1","source":"Deuring's identity for $C_d$","parts":[["text","Deuring's identity for "],["math","\\(C_d\\)"]]},"route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/deuring/index.html#deuring-identity"},{"id":"rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-small-primes","title":"Deuring's identity at the primes $2$, $p\\mid d$ and $p\\equiv3\\pmod4$","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.sum_quadraticChar_cd_eq_zero, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.card_cd_affine_of_mod_four_eq_three, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.cdCoeff_prime_of_mod_four_eq_three, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.deuring_prime_of_mod_four_eq_three, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.deuring_prime_of_dvd, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.deuring_two","summary":"Let $c_d(n)$ be the coefficients of the standard Euler product, $\\lambda_d(n)$ the Hecke coefficients, and for a prime $p$ let $\\left(\\frac{\\cdot}{p}\\right)$ be the quadratic character of $\\mathbb F_p$ (with value $0$ at $0$).","reading_title":{"format":"inline-parts-v1","source":"Deuring's identity at the primes $2$, $p\\mid d$ and $p\\equiv3\\pmod4$","parts":[["text","Deuring's identity at the primes "],["math","\\(2\\)"],["text",", "],["math","\\(p\\mid d\\)"],["text"," and "],["math","\\(p\\equiv3\\pmod4\\)"]]},"route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/deuring/index.html#deuring-small-primes"},{"id":"rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-of-euler-product","title":"Deuring's identity from the Euler product and the split primes","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.cdCoeff_prime_eq, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.deuringCd_of_heckeEuler, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.GaussSplit, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.deuringCd_of_heckeEuler_gaussSplit","summary":"Let $c_d(n)$ be the coefficients of the standard Euler product with Euler polynomials $P_{d,p}$, and $\\lambda_d(n)$ the Hecke coefficients. *Gauss's theorem at the split primes* holds for $d$ if $c_d(p)=\\lambda_d(p)$ for every prime $p\\equiv1\\pmod4$ with $p\\nmid d$.","route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/deuring/index.html#deuring-of-euler-product"},{"id":"rank/literature/hecke/deuring/gauss-split-twist","title":"The split primes for $C_d$ from the curve $y^2=x^3-x$","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.card_cd_affine_eq, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.sum_quadraticChar_twist, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.gaussSplit_of_one, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.gaussSplit_one_of_pointCount","summary":"For a prime $p$, $\\left(\\frac{\\cdot}{p}\\right)$ is the quadratic character of $\\mathbb F_p$ (with value $0$ at $0$). *Gauss's theorem at the split primes* for $d$ is as in Deuring's identity from the Euler product, and Gauss's point count is the statement about $y^2=x^3-x$ named there.","reading_title":{"format":"inline-parts-v1","source":"The split primes for $C_d$ from the curve $y^2=x^3-x$","parts":[["text","The split primes for "],["math","\\(C_d\\)"],["text"," from the curve "],["math","\\(y^2=x^3-x\\)"]]},"route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/deuring/index.html#gauss-split-twist"},{"id":"rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-from-gauss-count","title":"Deuring's identity for $d\\equiv1\\pmod4$ from Gauss's point count","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.deuringCd_of_gaussPointCount","summary":"If Gauss's point count holds, then Deuring's identity holds for every squarefree natural number $d\\equiv1\\pmod4$.","reading_title":{"format":"inline-parts-v1","source":"Deuring's identity for $d\\equiv1\\pmod4$ from Gauss's point count","parts":[["text","Deuring's identity for "],["math","\\(d\\equiv1\\pmod4\\)"],["text"," from Gauss's point count"]]},"route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/deuring/index.html#deuring-from-gauss-count"}],"result_edges":[["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-identity",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-of-euler-product","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-identity",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-small-primes","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-identity",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/gauss-split-twist","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-identity",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-of-euler-product",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/gauss-split-twist","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-of-euler-product",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-of-euler-product","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-small-primes",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/gauss-split-twist",0,1]],"boundary_edges":[["rank/literature/hecke/every-d/continuation-squarefree","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-from-gauss-count",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/continuation-of-deuring","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-identity",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/functional-equation-of-deuring","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-identity",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-of-euler-product",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/continuation-of-deuring","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-of-euler-product",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/gaussian/hecke-coefficients-non-split","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/deuring-small-primes",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/deuring/gauss-split-twist",0,1],["rank/literatu